## Current Synthesis

### Idea

Make the 100k view a first-class Tool Shed Project Executive View: the easy-to-find, easy-to-read
whole-project control surface that captures how the project's world picture changes, lets the
operator choose which cycles to undertake next, feeds selected outcomes into Ideas, direct work,
PRMs, and campaigns, and requires every material concern to remain accounted for until explicitly
resolved or dispositioned.

The operator is the CEO; the 100k view is the CEO's control surface. It sits above individual
Ideas and PRMs and reconciles their contribution to the project's current definition of
completion.

### Why It Matters

Projects can accumulate many Ideas, project maps, PRMs, campaigns, direct outcomes, evidence
records, and deferred obligations that all intend to advance the project. Existing indexes and
cycle views expose those records but do not provide one clear world view explaining the target
state, current landscape, material changes, strategic gaps, competing priorities, and best next
cycles. Important work can therefore be overlooked, duplicated, or considered complete merely
because it moved into another artifact.

The manually maintained `100,000-Foot View` in the DisplayTest firmware workspace demonstrates the
operator value of a North Star, landscape, ordered priority board, Idea Radar, deliberate non-goals,
realized outcomes, and review triggers. Its use also shows that a standard implementation must
prevent drift with existing Tool Shed state.

### Desired Outcome

Every Tool Shed project that needs strategic coordination can maintain one active Executive View
with a concise executive page and a complete underlying strategic ledger. The view shows why the
project exists, its current completion horizon, health by enduring responsibility, material
changes, current priorities, decisions needed, recommended next cycles, active strategic
descendants, deferred obligations, and realized outcomes.

Every material 100k item has a stable identity and explicit disposition or downstream relationship.
Every strategic Idea, PRM, campaign, or direct outcome maps back to the view or is explicitly
classified outside its scope. Completion results and residual gaps return to the view. A review
revision cannot be reconciled while an item, relationship, result, or material project area has
been silently skipped.

## Constraints And Non-Goals

- Architectural prerequisite: `IDEA-0027` delivered the schema-version-2 shared project projection,
  dashboard consumer convergence, measured line-debt repayment, and explicit 100k replacement
  boundary in Tool Shed v0.54.0. The 100k implementation must consume that released seam.
- The feature must reuse existing identity, document revision, relationship, outcome-cycle,
  recursive-closure, evidence, finding, and project-projection mechanisms wherever adequate.
- It must replace or consolidate overlapping project-map, focus-area, overview, status, navigation,
  or dashboard assembly rather than create another independent authority or reporting family.
- Keep the executive page short and readable while retaining an exhaustive, machine-checkable
  ledger beneath or behind it.
- The operator selects direction. Tool Shed may identify gaps, conflicts, and safe next choices but
  must not invent priorities or material decisions.
- Promotion into an Idea or PRM is not completion. The originating 100k item remains open or
  in-cycle until results and remaining gaps return.
- An explicit deferral, decline, supersession, or monitoring condition is valid accounting; forcing
  complete accounting must not force implementation of every possible idea.
- Settled product truth remains in project docs, README files, and code. The Executive View is
  evolving project direction under `work/`.

## Possibilities And Tradeoffs

| Possibility | Benefits | Costs / Risks | Evidence / Status |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Concise executive page plus exhaustive strategic ledger | Keeps the normal review readable without sacrificing complete accounting | Requires careful separation of synthesis from source facts | Preferred product shape |
| Focus areas as the coverage partition | Gives “whole picture” a bounded, project-specific completeness basis | Focus-area boundaries may be incomplete or stale | Reuse and potentially absorb the existing focus-area presentation |
| Bidirectional artifact reconciliation | Prevents 100k items or active strategic work from disappearing | Scope must exclude irrelevant low-level tasks | Reuse existing relationships, findings, and closure machinery |
| Current completion horizon within a permanent view | Allows releases or target states to finish even when the product continues | Horizon changes require explicit operator decisions | Preferred lifecycle model |
| One shared project projection for local and hosted surfaces | Reduces drift and can delete duplicate overview assembly | Depends on IDEA-0027 architecture | Required simplification dependency |
| Standardize the DisplayTest document directly | Builds on observed operator value | Copying its long narrative unchanged could create an encyclopedia | Use as a dogfood source, not an unquestioned universal template |

