## Decisions

- Treat the operator as CEO and the 100k view as the CEO's project control surface.
- Treat 100k as a distinct first-class product role above individual Ideas and PRMs, while requiring
  implementation reuse rather than a separate subsystem.
- Use `Project Executive View` as the formal product name and `100k` as its stable operator command,
  nickname, and easy-to-find `work/100k.md` projection.
- Make `work/100k.md` a deterministic read-only projection, not another authority. Operator intent,
  priorities, and dispositions remain in existing project maps, focus areas, Ideas, PRMs, campaigns,
  outcomes, and decisions; the view detects and exposes incomplete accounting across them.
- Reuse existing document lifecycles, relationships, outcomes, reconciliation, recursive closure,
  planning order, and loop findings as the item state model. Do not create a 100k-specific lifecycle
  engine or free-standing strategic backlog.
- Absorb the human-facing summary responsibilities of overview, queue status/next, planning order,
  focus-area coverage, and loop-finding views into one executive page while retaining their machine
  APIs as drill-down and automation surfaces.
- Treat source revision, domain digest, active lifecycle changes, planning-order changes, focus-area
  coverage drift, outcome/reconciliation changes, and loop findings as review-change signals.
- Keep the Executive View permanently active; reconcile individual review revisions or completion
  horizons instead of terminally completing the living view.
- Use a two-layer presentation: concise executive page first, complete strategic ledger second.
- Require explicit result feedback and residual-work disposition before a promoted item can close.
- Track this capability separately from, and make it dependent on, `IDEA-0027`.

